# Privacy Policy for Sunny-side

**Effective Date:** July 29, 2025  
**Last Updated:** July 29, 2025

## Introduction

Saturn Ventures ("we," "our," or "us") operates the Sunny-side mobile application (the "Service"). This privacy policy explains how we collect, use, and protect your information when you use our Service.

## Information We Collect

### Location Information
- **Device Location**: We access your device's GPS location to calculate sun position and provide seating recommendations
- **Address Information**: When you enter departure and destination addresses, we use them for journey planning
- **Usage**: Location data is used only for sun calculations and is not stored permanently

### Information We Don't Collect
- **No Personal Data**: We do not collect names, emails, phone numbers, or other personal identifiers
- **No Account Required**: Our app works without registration or login
- **No Tracking**: We do not track your usage patterns or behavior
- **No Advertising Data**: We do not collect data for advertising purposes

## How We Use Information

### Primary Functions
- Calculate sun position based on your location and time
- Provide seating recommendations to avoid direct sunlight
- Convert addresses to coordinates for journey planning
- Determine local time zones for accurate calculations

### External Services
We use the following free services to provide our functionality:
- **Nominatim/Photon**: For address geocoding (converting addresses to coordinates)
- **BigDataCloud/TimeZoneDB**: For timezone and local time information

## Data Storage and Security

- **Local Processing**: Most calculations are performed locally on your device
- **No Cloud Storage**: We do not store your location data or search history in the cloud
- **Temporary Data**: Location and address data are used temporarily for calculations only
- **Secure Transmission**: API requests to external services use secure HTTPS connections

## Third-Party Services

Our app integrates with external geocoding and timezone services. These services have their own privacy policies:
- Nominatim (OpenStreetMap Foundation)
- Photon (OpenStreetMap)
- BigDataCloud
- TimeZoneDB

We recommend reviewing their privacy policies for information about how they handle location data.

## Your Rights and Choices

- **Location Permissions**: You can disable location access in your device settings at any time
- **Data Deletion**: Since we don't store personal data, there's no data to delete
- **App Removal**: Uninstalling the app removes all local data

## Children's Privacy

Our Service does not address anyone under the age of 13. We do not knowingly collect personally identifiable information from children under 13.

## Changes to Privacy Policy

We may update our Privacy Policy from time to time. We will notify you of any changes by posting the new Privacy Policy on this page and updating the "Last Updated" date.

## International Users

Our app is available worldwide. Location data processing occurs locally on your device, with minimal data sent to geocoding services for address conversion.

## Contact Information

If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, please contact us:

